'''Lee Arenberg''' {{born|18|July|1962}} is an actor who played {{dis|Gral|Ferengi}} in the {{s|DS9}} [[DS9 Season 1|first season]] episode {{e|The Nagus}}, [[Prak]] in the {{s|TNG}} [[TNG Season 7|seventh season]] episode {{e|Force of Nature}}, [[Bok]] later that season in {{e|Bloodlines}}, [[Pelk]] in the {{s|VOY}} [[VOY Season 5|fifth season]] episode {{e|Juggernaut}}, and {{dis|Gral|Tellarite}} in the {{s|ENT}} [[DS9 Season 4|fourth season]] episodes {{e|United}} and {{e|The Aenar}}.

For "Juggernaut", Arenberg filmed his scenes between Monday {{d|18|January|1999}} and Monday {{d|25|January|1999}} on [[Paramount Stage 8]], [[Paramount Stage 9|9]], and [[Paramount Stage 16|16]].

Born in Palo Alto, California, he appeared in numerous films and television series, ranging from ''Scrubs'' to {{wt|CSI: Crime Scene Investigation}} (2001, starring [[Paul Guilfoyle]], with [[Kelly Connell]], [[Alicia Coppola]], [[Kellie Waymire]] and [[Albie Selznick]]). He also played Pintel, one of the sinister undead pirates in the films ''Pirates of the Caribbean: The Curse of the Black Pearl'', ''Pirates of the Caribbean: Dead Man's Chest'', and ''Pirates of the Caribbean: At World's End'' with co-star [[Vanessa Branch]] and stuntman [[Tom Morga]]. 

Arenberg once guest-starred in {{wt|Live Shot}}. Other ''Star Trek'' stars who were cast members include [[David Birney]], [[Karen Austin]], [[Ron Canada]], [[Jeff Yagher]], [[Bruce McGill]], and [[Sam Anderson]]. ''Star Trek'' performers who also guest-starred include [[Casey Biggs]], [[Chase Masterson]], [[Dion Anderson]], [[John Schuck]], [[Hal Landon, Jr.]], [[Cully Fredricksen]], and [[Kenneth Tigar]]. In two different seasons of ''Seinfeld'', he appeared in the same role. ''Voyager'' guest [[Jason Alexander]] was on camera with him in the first episode he made. He recurred on {{wt|Once Upon a Time (TV series)|Once Upon a Time}} as Grumpy/Leroy for its first six seasons. Arenberg also appeared on {{wt|American Gods}} (2019, featuring [[Corbin Bernsen]], [[Fionnula Flanagan]], and [[Scott Thompson]]). 

