'''Stephen Davies''' {{born|18|June|1950}} is an actor who guest starred in three episodes of the two ''Star Trek'' spin-off series {{s|DS9}} and {{s|VOY}}. The jacket worn by him in the [[VOY Season 3|third season]] episode {{e|Darkling}} was sold off on the [[It's A Wrap! sale and auction]] on eBay and also re-used in several ''Deep Space Nine'' episodes. {{stala|9308}}

Davies started his acting career in the 1970s and has appeared in films such as {{wt|Inserts (film)|Inserts}} (1974), ''The Hostage Heart'' (1977, with [[Sharon Acker]], [[Bob Minor]] and [[Ed McCready]]), {{wt|Heart Beat (film)|Heart Beat}} (1980, with [[John Larroquette]] and [[John Hostetter]]), {{wt|The Razor's Edge (1984 film)|The Razor's Edge}} (1984, with [[Catherine Hicks]]), {{wt|The Hanoi Hilton (film)|The Hanoi Hilton}} (1987, with [[David Soul]], [[Lawrence Pressman]], [[John Vargas]], [[Rick Fitts]], [[Brian Demonbreun]] and [[Bill Cho Lee]]), ''Rage and Honor'' (1992, with [[Brian Thompson]], [[Alex Datcher]], [[Tim de Zarn]] and [[Faith Minton]]), {{wt|Alien Intruder}} (1993, starring [[Jeff Conaway]] and [[Tracy Scoggins]], with [[Joe Durrenberger]] and [[Bill Zuckert]]), {{wt|Dillinger and Capone}} (1995, starring [[Martin Sheen]], with [[F. Murray Abraham]], Catherine Hicks, [[Anthony Crivello]], [[Jeffrey Combs]], [[Time Winters]], [[Clint Howard]], [[Bert Remsen]], [[Jeffrey Dean Morgan]], [[Jessica Hendra]] and [[Debi A. Monahan]]), {{wt|Scene of the Crime (1996 film)|Scene of the Crime}} (1996, with Tim de Zarn), and ''Star Portal'' (1998, with [[Athena Massey]] and Anthony Crivello). Several films he played in were produced by {{w|Roger Corman}}.

He has also performed in television series such as {{wt|Starsky & Hutch}} (1976, starring David Soul), {{wt|Dallas (TV series)|Dallas}} (1978, directed by [[Lawrence Dobkin]]), {{wt|CHiPs}} (1981, with [[Robert Pine]] and [[Marc Alaimo]]), {{wt|Scarecrow and Mrs. King}} (1984, starring [[Kate Jackson]]), ''The Secret World of Alex Mack'' (1995), and [[J.J. Abrams]]' {{wt|Alias (TV series)|Alias}} (2002, starring [[Merrin Dungey]] and [[Victor Garber]], with [[Stephen Mendillo]] and [[Terry O'Quinn]]).

