'''Pablo Soriano''' {{born|2|June|1957}} is an actor, dancer, and choreographer who was a regular background performer throughout the run of {{s|DS9}}, {{s|VOY}}, and {{s|ENT}}. He appeared as several [[Jem'Hadar]], [[Borg]], [[Bajoran]]s, [[Cardassian]]s, [[Tellarite]]s, and [[Klingon]]s. In addition, he worked as a [[stand-in]] for regulars and guest actors.

Soriano appeared as an EMT in the ''ER'' episodes "The Gift" (1994, with [[Kevin Michael Richardson]], [[Paul Eiding]], [[Jeanette Miller]], [[Star Halm]], and [[Melissa Vinicor]]), "Long Day's Journey" (1995, with [[Sam Anderson]], [[Kathleen Garrett]], [[Dennis Howard]], [[Lily Mariye]], [[Byron Thames]], [[Brian Cousins]], and Melissa Vinicor), "Feb 5, '95" (1995, with [[Christine Harnos]], [[Tommy 'Tiny' Lister, Jr.]], Lily Mariye, and Melissa Vinicor), "Make of Two Hearts" (1995, with [[Meg Foster]], [[Mike Genovese]], Sam Anderson, [[Kimberly Auslander]], and Melissa Vinicor), and "The Birthday Party" (1995, with Christine Harnos, [[Mark Rolston]], [[Stephen Rowe]], Lily Mariye, [[Christopher Darga]], [[John Chandler]], [[Todd Merrill]], [[Robert Cox]], and Melissa Vinicor), as a cinema patron in ''Seinfeld'' (1996), as a cop in the television movie ''The Second Civil War'' (1997, with [[Joanna Cassidy]], [[Ron Perlman]], [[William Schallert]], and Robert Picardo) and as Colonel Soliz in {{wt|Kingpin (TV series)|Kingpin}} (2003, starring [[Sheryl Lee]], with [[L. Sidney]] and [[Jorge Cervera, Jr.]]). He was also credited as choreographer for {{wt|Resurrection Blvd.}} (2000-02, with [[Ray Wise]] and [[Lawrence Monoson]]) and appeared as a pizza delivery guy in the pilot episode of ''Veronica Mars'' (2004).

Soriano also had a guest role in the television series ''Secretos'' (2008) and appeared as a regular principal actor, Detective Ramos, in several episodes of {{wt|Dexter (TV series)|Dexter}} (2006-08, alongside [[Keith Carradine]]). He was also a day player on ''Reno 911!'', where he appeared as a Mexican police officer, and was a lead dancer on [[CBS Broadcasting|CBS]]' {{wt|Clubhouse (TV series)|Clubhouse}}.

