'''Rolando "J.R." Quinonez''' is an artist and actor who was the regular [[stand-in]], [[body double]], and [[photo double]] for [[Robert Picardo]] on {{s|VOY}} and for [[John Billingsley]] on {{s|ENT}}. His only credited appearance was in the episode {{e|Renaissance Man}} as [[Hologram Overlooker 001|Overlooker/Doctor]]. Quinonez also portrayed the original, non speaking version of {{dis|Kol|Ferengi}} in the {{s|TNG}} [[TNG Season 3|third season]] episode {{e|The Price}}.

Picardo spoke in an interview about his work with Quinonez in {{e|Life Line}} during shooting for the special effects sequence, where he was Picardo's on-screen photo double. Quinonez played also a role in a ''Star Trek: Enterprise'' episode where he wore the costume from [[Tom Morga]] as [[Minnis]] in {{e|Alliances}}. This information is from the costumer's tag and the costume was sold off on [[It's A Wrap! sale and auction]] on eBay. Other costumes which were sold off on the It's A Wrap! auction were Quinonez' photo double costumes from the episode {{e|Virtuoso}} {{stala|9415}} and another episode. {{stala|3690}}

Quinonez' other credits are as a casting associate in ''Blind Side'' (1993, with [[Jonathan Banks]], [[Jorge Cervera, Jr.]], [[Josh Cruze]], and stunts by [[Jimmy Ortega]]), as a production assistant in ''World Inside Me'' (1998, written, directed, produced and starring ''Star Trek'' visual effects coordinator/supervisor [[David Takemura]] and with [[Maya Fujimoto]]), as a production assistant in {{wt|Dear John (American TV series)|Dear John}} (1988-1992), and as a production staff member in the pilot episode of {{wt|Committed (American TV series)|Committed}} (2005).

In the position of a stand-in he also worked on {{wt|Just Legal}} (2005-2006, guest starring [[Patti Yasutake]], [[Julie Warner]], [[Raphael Sbarge]], and stunt coordinated by [[Vince Deadrick, Jr.]]), ''Teachers'' (2006, starring [[Matt Winston]]), and the pilot episode of ''Dirt'' (2007, starring [[Jeffrey Nordling]] and [[Mariette Hartley]]).

